---
date: 2025-06-23T00:00:00-04:00
---

The Quorum is a building on the [[Geography/Star 221,325|Joker World at Star 221,325]], raised of black metal and living vine. The metal is a [[Sky Metal|sky metal]], reflective and formed at least in part by magic. Four corner towers carry greenish-blue braziers, the only steady light on the plateau. Tents left by an earlier Scale scouting party stand outside, and beyond them a single door twenty feet tall, cut into the wall with no hinges and no handle. It speaks to those who approach, shaping letters out of wrought metal and twisted vine, and asks whether they would descend to save a soul tormented by captors.

Inside, the building is filled with lava. Three staircases descend into it from a landing just inside the door, and the air carries copper and brimstone. A monolith on the landing holds three gears; a crankshaft turns a gear and pulls a stopper free, and the lava drains down to uncover the stairs and the rooms below. Vines run out of the lava along the back wall and up through a pane of the glass roof.

[[Flintlock Toboggan]] is chained in a small room off the stairs, its walls, floor and glass ceiling covered in runic circles in an old Celestial script. Past the lava is a hall where [[Sigzil Haight]]'s fiends gather, with a fountain of blood at one end. Flintlock says the Quorum is an assembly hall, and that it is not supposed to be here.

The fountain of blood is a two-way portal. Shutting off its flow severs the passage into Sigzil Haight's demesne on the far side; opening it again lets a traveler walk in. The door of the Quorum shapes its questions to anyone who approaches and asks whether they will delve deeper to save a lost soul.
